<title>FRANCE: Casino H1 net attrib rises 45 pct.</title>
<headline>Casino H1 net attrib rises 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			 294	vs	 203</p>
<p>    Net						325  vs	     223</p>
<p>    Net attributable per share (francs)   3.74  vs	    2.67</p>
<p>    Operating					564  vs	     522</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		   404  vs	     314</p>
<p>    Exceptional gains			     70  vs		20</p>
<p>    Cashflow					 901  vs	     816</p>
<p>    Investments				    958  vs	     897</p>
<p>    Turnover				    31,630  vs	  30,082</p>
<p>NOTE - Casino said in a statement that net attributable profit rose 44.8 percent in the first half, and operating profit rose eight percent.</p>
<p>It said the gains reflected in part the growth of Casino USA as well as higher profitability in France.</p>
<p>It said it planned to open its first store in Poland before the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
